{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>לֹא יִהְיֶה לַכֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹ׳ וְנַחֲלָה לֹא יִהְיֶה וְגוֹ׳.</b> The verse repeats the matter to say that even if they transgressed and gave them an inheritance, that inheritance will not stand to their merit — and this is what it says, <b>וְנַחֲלָה לֹא יִהְיֶה</b> etc. And the reason for the juxtaposition of this commandment to the commandment of the king is to say that the king is equal to the people in the commandments stated regarding the matter of giving them their gifts, and his heart is not to be lifted up above his brethren so as to turn aside from the commandment that HaShem commands for the entirety of Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:55.898663234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}